**MedSync Health Raises $85 Million in Series C Funding to Transform Care Coordination**

**BOSTON, MA – December 15, 2024** – MedSync Health, a leader in AI-powered care coordination, today announced that it has closed an $85 million Series C funding round. The round was led by a new, undisclosed investor, with participation from existing investors.

The new funding will be used to accelerate MedSync Health’s growth, including expanding its sales and marketing efforts, investing in product development, and expanding into new geographic markets.

“We are thrilled to have the support of our new and existing investors as we continue to build the future of care coordination,” said Dr. Evelyn Reed, CEO of MedSync Health. “This funding will allow us to accelerate our mission of connecting hospitals, clinics, and patients through real-time data integration and AI-powered workflows.”

MedSync Health has experienced rapid growth since its founding in 2018. The company now serves over 140 hospitals and health systems in the US and Europe. The MedSync Platform has been shown to reduce readmissions, improve care team communication, and lower costs.

“MedSync Health is solving a critical problem in healthcare,” said a representative from the lead investor. “We are impressed with the company’s technology, team, and vision, and we are excited to partner with them on their next phase of growth.”

**About MedSync Health**

MedSync Health is a healthcare technology company that provides a care coordination platform for hospitals and health systems. The company’s mission is to connect hospitals, clinics, and patients through real-time data integration and AI-powered workflows. MedSync Health is a Series C startup backed by leading venture capital firms.

